id:                     E6405
trigger_tool:           Conan|Meson|pkg-config|linker
phase:                  configure|link|dependency-closure
error_signature:        dependency found and headers compile but linker reports undefined symbols because generated pkg-config Libs is empty
severity:               2
category:               build,conan,meson,pkg-config,linker,dependency,evidence
match_keywords:         undefined symbol, SDLNet_, SDL2_net.pc, pkg-config Libs, dependency found, link closure
title:                  Conan dependency metadata must bind header and linker contracts together

root_cause:             Meson can report a dependency as found when pkg-config provides a version and include directory, while an incomplete package metadata record emits no library in Libs. The consumer then compiles headers successfully but fails at final link with undefined provider symbols. Header-layout repair alone cannot establish a link closure.
affected_scope:        Conan consumers of C/C++ packages whose published cpp_info or pkg-config metadata omits the provider library, especially packages with a renamed or case-sensitive pkg-config module.
verification_cmd:      Bind the exact dependency package revision; verify the public header and provider library under the package folder; force the canonical pkg-config module name before generation; inspect generated Cflags and Libs; require a production link that resolves provider symbols.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           generated-pkgconfig-link-closure
rec_description:        Use a task-local metadata normalizer only when the package folder proves both header and library presence. Set the module name expected by the consumer, append exactly one provider library flag, and fail closed on missing or malformed metadata.
rec_command:            inspect generated <module>.pc and production linker command; rebuild with the same package revision
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               Conan generate() repair bound to dependency package folder and module name

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      source-level-link-argument
fallback_description:   A Meson link argument may be used only when the dependency cannot expose a safe pkg-config record and the library path/name is fixed by an explicit package contract; prefer metadata repair to avoid duplicate or platform-specific flags.
fallback_command:       add one exact provider library argument under the feature's found() guard
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:           Meson dependency declaration

forbid_1_pattern:       treat dependency().found() or successful header compilation as proof of link closure
forbid_1_reason:        Discovery and Cflags can succeed while Libs is empty or names the wrong module.
forbid_1_consequence:   Undefined provider symbols appear only at the final executable link and can be misclassified as an ABI or compiler failure.
forbid_2_pattern:       append arbitrary -l flags without verifying the task-owned package folder|disable the feature to avoid linking
forbid_2_reason:        An unverified library name can select a foreign system object, while disabling the feature hides a broken published dependency.
forbid_2_consequence:   The binary may link against the wrong provider or silently omit required networking functionality.

principles:             P005,P010,P013
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E6404]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

